4,1,,status,Asuka,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
5,1,1,talk,Asuka,,We need to verify staffing capacity before discussing any new routes. Who is checking the roster books?,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
6,1,1,talk,Takumi,,"I’m checking the timed runs and crowd counts. The stopwatch tells the truth, not the complaints.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
7,1,1,talk,Benjamin,,I’m reviewing the capital ledger balances. Headline totals are meaningless if we ignore the long-term commitments they lock in.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
8,1,1,talk,Servas,,I am reading the joint operators' committee minutes. We must understand who holds the final say before we promise anything.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
9,1,1,talk,Jonathan,,I am checking the contingency pricing inside the pre-war shells. The ground often hides what the drawings miss.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
10,1,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Benjamin, does the ledger show if the operating subsidy can actually absorb the overtime costs we are already seeing?","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
11,1,2,talk,Takumi,,"@Asuka, the stopwatch shows the mid-city route is slower, but the platforms clear at the old rate. The bottleneck isn't the crowd, it's the wait.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
12,1,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Asuka, the ledger shows the operating subsidy was trimmed again. It cannot absorb new overtime without cutting maintenance.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
13,1,2,talk,Servas,,"@Jonathan, the minutes show the ferry and rail back offices never agreed on common data terms. That silence will stall any integrated plan.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
14,1,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Servas, that silence is exactly why I’m checking the shells. If the data won’t flow, the ground better not surprise us either.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
15,1,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Takumi, if the platforms clear at the old rate, then the delay is in the connections. We need to audit where the minutes actually go.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
16,1,3,talk,Takumi,,"@Asuka, exactly. The stopwatch proves the surface route is the problem, not the platforms. We need to stop guessing and measure the actual wait times.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
17,1,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Asuka, the ledger confirms the technology line was also trimmed. We cannot fund new systems without cutting existing maintenance.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
18,1,3,talk,Servas,,"@Benjamin, the ledger is a map of what we have, not what we need. We must look at the crew establishment to see if we have the hands to do the work.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
19,1,3,talk,Jonathan,,"@Servas, the hands are thin, but the ground is the real trap. I’m checking the pre-war shells to see what voids are waiting for us.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
20,1,4,talk,Asuka,,"@Benjamin, if the technology line is cut, we cannot promise a new fare system. We must prioritize what the existing crews can actually maintain.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
21,1,4,talk,Takumi,,"@Asuka, agreed. But we must also check the late-turn rosters. If the pool is empty, extending hours is just a fantasy.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
22,1,4,talk,Benjamin,,"@Takumi, the late-turn pool is indeed thinning. But @Asuka, remember, the capital ledger still holds a ring-fenced construction balance from a lapsed grant.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Takumi"",""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
23,1,4,talk,Servas,,"@Benjamin, that ring-fenced balance is a ghost. It belongs to a lapsed grant, not our current needs. We must not build on phantom money.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
24,1,4,talk,Jonathan,,"@Servas, phantoms or not, the voids in the shells are real. I am checking the contingency pricing to see how much that silence costs us.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
25,1,,action,Asuka,,Roster books for the late-turn pool; Crew establishment and maintenance contract,"{""action"":""investigate"",""cards"":[""card_09"",""card_10""],""parse"":""ok""}"
