34,2,,status,Asuka,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"@Benjamin, the roster books confirm the late-turn pool is critically thin. Overtime is already covering overnight works. We cannot extend hours without breaking the existing schedule.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Takumi,,#### Turn 2 of 4,"{""words"":5,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,#### Turn 2 of 4,"{""words"":5,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Servas,,#### Turn 2 of 4,"{""words"":5,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,#### Turn 2 of 4,"{""words"":5,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Asuka,,#### Turn 2 of 4,"{""words"":5,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Takumi,,"@Asuka, the journey audits confirm your suspicion. Most added minutes are spent waiting for connections, not paying. The machines are fine; the schedule is broken.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Takumi, the audit confirms the wait is the cost. But @Asuka, the crew establishment shows roadway crews are a third below target. We lack the hands to fix the schedule.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Takumi"",""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Servas,,#### Turn 2 of 4,"{""words"":5,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Benjamin, the completion records show the accessibility rebuilds finished on time, but the lane-priority stretches failed. We have the hands for lifts, not for roads.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Benjamin, if the roadway crews are depleted, we cannot build the dedicated lanes. We must focus on what the existing maintenance contract can actually support.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Takumi,,"@Benjamin, the crews are thin, but the audit proves the wait is the killer. We need to fix the connections, not just the pavement.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Takumi, fixing connections requires data integration, which the technology line cannot fund. @Servas, did the old pilots prove we can do this cheaply?","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Takumi"",""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Servas,,"@Benjamin, the late-evening pilot met its cost target, but the ferry trial failed on data terms. We cannot assume old success applies to new integration.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"@Benjamin, the data failure is a warning, not a verdict. The accessibility records prove we can deliver physical upgrades on time. Let us build what we can actually maintain.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Asuka,,"@Jonathan, physical upgrades are viable, but @Benjamin, the maintenance contract has spare capacity for lifts. We should prioritize station access over anything requiring new roadway crews.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Jonathan"",""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Takumi,,"@Asuka, if the lifts work, the platforms clear faster. But the audit says the wait is the killer. We need to fix the connections, not just the stairs.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"@Takumi, the audit blames the wait, but the ledger says we can’t afford the data integration to fix it. @Asuka, the lift capacity is the only viable path.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Takumi"",""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Servas,,"@Benjamin, the ledger is a cage, but the pilots show the door. We must choose the path that respects both the money and the memory.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,"@Benjamin, the cage is real, but the lift contract has room. Let us build the access, not the fantasy.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
