63,3,1,talk,Servas,,"- **Servas**: The candidates are before us. Let us weigh them against the evidence we have gathered, not against our hopes.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,"- **Jonathan**: @Servas, agreed. The evidence points to physical access. Let us not let the data ghosts scare us from the solid ground.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"- **Asuka**: @Jonathan, the evidence supports Station Access Upgrades. The lift contract has capacity, and the crews can deliver it without breaking the budget.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Takumi,,"- **Takumi**: @Asuka, I object. The audit proves the wait is the killer. Station access doesn't fix broken connections. I vote for the Crosstown Corridor.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Takumi, the corridor requires roadway crews we do not have. The ledger forbids it. I vote for Station Access Upgrades.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Servas,,"@Takumi, the corridor is a fantasy the crews cannot build. I vote for Station Access Upgrades, where the hands and the money actually meet.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Takumi, the records show lane-priority failed before. We cannot repeat that error. I vote for Station Access Upgrades.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Asuka,,"- **Asuka**: @Takumi, the corridor is a fantasy the crews cannot build. I vote for Station Access Upgrades, where the hands and the money actually meet.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Takumi,,"- **Takumi**: @Asuka, I stand by the audit. The wait is the cost. I vote for the Crosstown Corridor, despite the risks.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Takumi, the audit is valid, but the ledger is absolute. We cannot fund a corridor we cannot staff. I stand by Station Access Upgrades.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Servas,,"@Takumi, the stopwatch is honest, but the ledger is stricter. We cannot build what we cannot staff. I vote for Station Access Upgrades.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Jonathan,,"@Takumi, the ground is solid, the crews are ready, and the budget holds. I vote for Station Access Upgrades.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Asuka,,"- **Asuka**: @Takumi, the evidence is clear. The crews can deliver access, not corridors. I vote for Station Access Upgrades.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Takumi,,"- **Takumi**: @Asuka, I respect the logic, but I cannot ignore the stopwatch. I vote for the Crosstown Corridor.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,"@Takumi, the ledger is absolute. We cannot fund a corridor we cannot staff. I stand by Station Access Upgrades.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Servas,,"@Takumi, the stopwatch is honest, but the ledger is stricter. We cannot build what we cannot staff. I vote for Station Access Upgrades.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Jonathan,,"@Takumi, the ground is solid, the crews are ready, and the budget holds. I vote for Station Access Upgrades.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
